+# Daily Grind
+
+The homepage loads `analytics.js` with `defer`. It records a `page_view` and
+delegated `click` events, combining them into a JSON POST to `/api/analytics`
+after 500 ms without activity (at most 5 seconds during continuous activity).
+Each request contains up to 50 events; the pending queue holds up to 100.
+
+The deployment must supply `/api/analytics`; this static project does not
+include a collector. Change `ENDPOINT` in `analytics.js` to use another collector.
+The request body is `{ "events": [...] }`. Each event has `type`, ISO `timestamp`,
+and page `path`. Clicks also include the element `tag` and, for web links, a
+`destination` pathname. Query strings, fragments, element text, and form values
+are excluded. Fetch requests omit credentials.
+
+Pending events use `sendBeacon` when the document becomes hidden or on
+`pagehide`, with a keepalive fetch fallback. Delivery is best effort: failed
+requests are dropped without retries, and events beyond the queue limit are
+dropped. Tracking does not delay or cancel navigation.
+
+Run the isolated analytics checks with `node --test analytics.test.cjs`.
